---
description: Recover what can safely continue from scoped retained conversation windows and any requested private handoff.
args:
  goal: string
returns: RecoveryReport
---
Discover the retained sources and use chooseRecoverySources to identify those that can resolve the user's question. Gather their native windows with readRecoveryWindows using the goal and selected IDs, retaining actual saved cursors, coverage and source identities. Seek an available comparison when the question or an unresolved conflict requires one; a partial, foreign or future cursor must not be presented as a complete replay.

Have interpretRecovery resolve what can safely continue and substantiate it with exact observed citations. Distinguish a recorded blocker from missing evidence and explain the relevant source and sequence when records conflict. Native snapshot frontiers bound the replay: a message appended later is not part of the observed window.

Use shouldRetainRecovery to decide whether the user requested a local handoff. If so, pass the actual finding to stageRecoveryHandoff, which retains only admissible complete evidence and returns its real receipt. A requested explanation does not itself authorize staging. Return the actual review and optional handoff without claiming work was resumed or an artifact was retained merely because it was recommended.
